   "date": "2014-10-28T21:39:45Z",
   "subject": "Silence SSL warnings",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello!<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m developing an app for which I use amazon EC2 as a backend, and query it using RCurl. My problem is that the backend has an SSL certificate that does not match the random ec2 instance name. I was able to run my queries locally using <div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> getURL</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data_url</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> curl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">curl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ssl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">verifypeer </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div>But when I deploy the app to <a href=\"http://shinyapp.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapp.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792364402558000&amp;usg=AOvVaw14P_vdOHHUu7guraKrSPa6\">shinyapp.io</a> it instantly crashes with the following error:<div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><div>Listening on <a href=\"http://127.0.0.1:53950\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://127.0.0.1:53950&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792364402558000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3CCrhk22o8yf7iGyKcBZX4\">http://127.0.0.1:53950</a></div><div>Loading required package: bitops</div><div>Error in function (type, msg, asError = TRUE)  : </div><div>  SSL: certificate subject name () does not match target host name &#39;<a href=\"http://ec2-xx-xxx-xxx-xx.compute-1.amazonaws.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ec2-xx-xxx-xxx-xx.compute-1.amazonaws.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792364402558000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Ajnas-5GpXVgpNXA9b5rG\">ec2-xx-xxx-xxx-xx.compute-1.amazonaws.com</a>&#39;</div></div></code></div><br></div><div>How can I bypass this issue?</div><div>Thank you,</div><div>Kirill.</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "vC0ou6BeviEJ",
   "from": "Andy Kipp",
   "author": "e84e7628b5f8a3e1",
   "date": "2014-11-03T15:48:49Z",
   "subject": "Re: [shinyapps-users] Silence SSL warnings",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I think you need to also do: ssl.verifyhost = FALSE<div><br></div><div>However please keep in mind you are exposing yourself to man-in the middle attacks.<br><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">-Andy</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
